        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Addressable status LEDs (WS2812B, D5-D7, D18-D21) and an analog switch (ISL54222AIUZ, U5) for LED/signal routing."}
      ],
      "impact": "The addressable WS2812B status LED strip receives no data; the LEDs stay off or latch an undefined state, so the board's intended status indication is lost.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The drawing is largely consistent with the spec (16 MHz CAN crystals, SM712-class TVS, ideal-diode USB path, open-drain e-stop buffers, separate 3.3 V_PI_OUT and +3V3 rails), but the TXS0101 level-shifter U21 that feeds the WS2812B status-LED data line has its OE pin shorted to ground, which permanently disables the level shifter and breaks the addressable-LED feature the spec intends."
